### VS Code REST Client (extension humao.rest-client). Start the server first: npm start
@root = http://localhost:3000
@base = {{root}}/api

### Health check -> 200
GET {{root}}/health

### List users -> 200
GET {{base}}/users

### Create a user -> 201
POST {{base}}/users
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Anna", "email": "anna@example.com", "role": "owner" }

### Invalid user -> 400 with details
POST {{base}}/users
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "", "email": "not-an-email" }

### One user -> 200
GET {{base}}/users/1

### Missing user -> 404
GET {{base}}/users/999

### Bad id -> 400
GET {{base}}/users/abc

### Partial update with PATCH -> 200
PATCH {{base}}/users/1
Content-Type: application/json

{ "role": "editor" }

### Replace with PUT -> 200
PUT {{base}}/users/1
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Ada King", "email": "ada@example.com", "role": "owner" }

### Create a project -> 201
POST {{base}}/projects
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Billing", "description": "Invoices and payments", "ownerId": 1 }

### Create a diagram -> 201
POST {{base}}/diagrams
Content-Type: application/json

{ "title": "Billing schema", "notation": "ERD", "code": "invoice -> payment", "projectId": 1 }

### Search, sort and page -> 200
GET {{base}}/diagrams?q=billing&sort=-title&page=1&limit=10

### Projects of one user -> 200
GET {{base}}/users/1/projects

### Projects of an unknown user -> 404
GET {{base}}/users/99/projects

### Diagrams of one project -> 200
GET {{base}}/projects/1/diagrams

### Publish a diagram -> 200
POST {{base}}/diagrams/1/publish

### Duplicate a diagram -> 201
POST {{base}}/diagrams/1/duplicate

### Delete a user who owns projects -> 409
DELETE {{base}}/users/1

### Delete a diagram -> 204
DELETE {{base}}/diagrams/1

### Unknown route -> 404
GET {{base}}/nothing

### An Accept header that cannot match JSON -> 406
GET {{base}}/users
Accept: text/html

### An unknown query key is rejected, not silently ignored -> 400 invalid_query
GET {{base}}/users?bogus=1

### PUT without "role" keeps the current role instead of resetting it to "viewer" -> 200
PUT {{base}}/users/2
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Alan Turing", "email": "alan@example.com" }

### Allowed methods -> 204
OPTIONS {{base}}/users

### Headers only -> 200
HEAD {{base}}/users

### Stale update refused -> 412
PATCH {{base}}/users/2
Content-Type: application/json
If-Match: W/"0000000000000000"

{ "name": "Alan T." }

### Roles: Ada (user 1) changes Alan's project -> 403 with a Request ID
PATCH {{base}}/projects/2
Content-Type: application/json
X-User-Id: 1

{ "name": "Not mine" }

### Roles: Ada deletes a project -> 403 (only an administrator may)
DELETE {{base}}/projects/1
X-User-Id: 1

### Roles: administrator deletes a diagram of any project -> 204
DELETE {{base}}/diagrams/3
X-User-Id: 1
X-Role: admin

### Error page for a browser -> HTML 404 with description and Request ID
GET {{root}}/nope
Accept: text/html
